      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Cost-on-demand locking is bogus.  Then every fucking Avatar maker would demand a public avatar be paid for.  COD - Cost-on-Delivery marking is probably a better system for that.  Then again I could see almost all avatar worlds going down in favor of Cost-on-Delivery by most artists.  Oh, you want a specific avatar?  Well why don't you pay for it?  Basically VRC would no longer be free, it would be freemium.  Every user would be basically stuck with default avatars made by the most prominent contributors to VRC unless they either paid a small amount for a public avatar or a greater amount for a custom one.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
